    "ls|LS16_S16_U_193": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 193 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.12.2018 \n \nPerformance Review of Central Universities \n \n \n*193.  SHRI P.K. KUNHALIKUTTY: \n           SHRI JYOTIRADITYA M. SCINDIA: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has recently decided to conduct a performance review \nof all the Central Universities across the country; \n(b) if so, the purpose thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government has since taken any steps to improve the standard of \neducation in all the Central Universities across the country and compete with global \nuniversities; and \n \n(d) if so, the details in this regard?     \n                                      \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n \n(a) to (d):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n****** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFFERED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 193 FOR 24.12 .2018 ASKED BY SHRI P.K. \nKUNHALIKUTTY AND SHRI JYOTIRADITYA M. SCINDIA REGARDING \nPERFORMANCE REVIEW OF CENTRAL UNIVERSITIES \n \n(a) & (b): Yes Madam, Government has been monitoring performance of Central \nUniversities as per the MoU signed in accordance with Rule 229 (xi) of the General \nFinancial Rules, 2017. \n \n Vice Chancellors of Central Universities under the Ministry of Human Resource \nDevelopment (MHRD) have submitted MoUs comprising, inter-alia, performance \nparameters of current academic year and corresponding targets for the next \nacademic ear. This is mutually acceptable arrangement and not one way direction to \nthe Central Universities and is aimed at increasing accountability, transparency and \nquality of education and consequently to improve the national and international \nranking of the Universities.  \n \nMHRD has recently reviewed half yearly performance of the Central Universities \nbased on the MoU parameters with respect to academic and research performance. \nThe main purpose of such a review was to improve the academic and research \nstandards of these Universities. \n \n(c) & (d): The UGC (Mandatory Assessment and Accreditation of Higher Educational \nInstitutions) Regulation, 2012, inter-alia, requ ires every higher educational institution, \nincluding Central Universities (CUs), to undergo the accreditation process from a \nrecognized accreditation agency in accordance with the procedure laid thereunder. \nAccordingly, every Central University has to undergo accreditation by the National \nAssessment and Accreditation Council (NAAC), Bangalore, which undertakes \naccreditation on various quality parameters, including academic/ instructional and \ninfrastructural parameters. NAAC accreditation is valid for five years, after which, the \nCentral Universities have to again apply for. \n \nThe UGC has issued the (Promotion and Ma intenance of Standards of Academic \nCollaboration) Regulations 2012, which provide a framework for academic \ncollaboration between India and foreign higher educational institutions. To encourage \nresearch and development in the country, UGC implements various schemes such as \nUniversities with Potential for Excellence (UPE), Colleges with Potential for \nExcellence (CPE), Special Assistance Progra mme (SAP), Centres with Potential for \nExcellence in a Particular Area (CPEPA) et c. The UGC has launched the scheme of \nFaculty Recharge Programme wherein candidates are selected through global \nadvertisements. Under the CV Raman Postdoctoral Fellowships Scheme the young \nfaculties are attached to United States of America (USA) Universities to enable them \nto work with USA Scientists in their respective area of specialization. \n \nGovernment has launched various initiatives like Annual Refresher Programme in \nTeaching (ARPIT), Impactful Policy Resear ch in Social Sciences (IMPRESS),  \nImpacting Research Innovation and Technology (IMPRINT), Students Promoting \nAwareness Of Research Knowledge (SPARK), etc. \n*****\n ",
    "ls|LS16_S16_U_194": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.†*194 \nANSWERED ON 24.12.2018 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF TOURIST CIRCUITS \n \n†*194. SHRI SANJAY HARIBHAU JADHAV:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has received any proposal from \nMaharashtra regarding the scheme for development of tourist \ncircuits and tourist places;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with the current status of these \nproposals;  \n(c)  the progress and achievements made so far in this regard; and  \n(d)  the details of the funds allocated and spent for this purpose? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(SHRI K.J. ALPHONS) \n \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n********\n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PART S (a) TO (d) OF  LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. †*194 ANSWERED ON 24.12.2018 REGARDING \nDEVELOPMENT OF TOURIST CIRCUITS \n \n(a) to (d): The Ministry of Tourism under the schemes of Swadesh \nDarshan, PRASHAD (National Mission on Pilgrimage Rejuvenation and \nSpiritual, Heritage Augmentation Drive), provides Central Financial \nAssistance to the State Governments/ Union Territory (UT) \nAdministrations for development of tourism infrastructure in the \ncountry. Submission of project prop osals by the State \nGovernments/UT Admi nistrations under the above schemes is a \ncontinuous process. The projects are sanctioned subject to \navailability of funds, liquidation of pending utilization certificates, \nsubmission of suitable detailed project reports and adherence to the \nrelevant scheme guidelines. \n \nThe details of projects sanctioned for the State of Maharashtra \nunder the above schemes during the years 2015 -16 to 2018 -19 are as \nbelow: \n(Rs. in crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nName of \nthe \nScheme \nYear Name of the Project Amount \nSanctioned \nAmount \nReleased \n1. Swadesh \nDarshan  \n2015-16 Development of \nSindhudurg under \nCoastal Circuit in \nMaharashtra  \n82.17 12.79 \n2. Swadesh \nDarshan  \n2018-19 Development of \nWaki- Adasa- \nDhapewada- \nParadsingha- Chota \nTaj Bagh - \nTelankhandi- Girad \nunder Spiritual \nCircuit in \nMaharashtra  \n54.01 0.00 \n3. PRASHAD 2017-18 Development of \nTrimbakeshwar \n37.81 0.00 \n \nAll the projects are under implementation stage. \n******** ",
    "ls|LS16_S16_U_195": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *195 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24th December, 2018 \n \nIrregularities by School Managements \n \n*195. PROF. RAVINDRA VISHWANATH GAIKWAD: \n SHRIMATI  BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether irregularities are being committed by the managements/owners of \n some private/public schools in enrolment, charging of hefty donation, \n arbitrary/ exorbitant fees, compulsory buying of uniform, books and stationery \n from these schools and if so, the reaction of the Government thereto; \n \n(b) whether the Government has asked for any response from such schools and \n if so, the number of schools which have given response in this regard along \n with the extent to which these responses are satisfactory; \n \n(c) the details of schools found guilty in this regard and the action taken against \n such schools; \n \n(d) the steps taken/being taken to remove/check such irregularities; and \n \n(e) whether the Government proposes to introduce a common syllabus and \n similar uniform in all the schools of the country and if so, the time by which the \n same is likely to be implemented? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO THE PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NUMBER \n *195 FOR 24.12.2018 ASKED BY  PROF. RAVINDRA \nVISHWANATH GAIKWAD AND SHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI  \nPATIL REGARDING  “IRREGULARITIES BY SCHOOL MANAGEMENTS”. \n \n***** \n \n(a): The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has informed that they  \nreceive sporadic complaints against its Independent affiliated schools with regard to \ncharging of hefty donation, arbitrary/exorbi tant fees, compulsory buying of uniform, \nbooks and stationery from these schools.  As and when such complaints are \nreceived, the Board takes appropriate action as per the provisions of the Affiliation \nBye-Laws. \n \n(b) and (c): A statement indicating the  number of complaints received during the \nlast three years  and action taken thereon is annexed at Annexure I.  \n \nd) The affiliated schools of CBSE are expected to follow provisions of its Affiliation and \nExamination Bye-Laws and in case of violation of these Bye-Laws, appropriate action is \ntaken by the Board which depends on the gravity of mistake committed by the school and \nincludes withdrawal of affiliation granted to the school. \n \ne)  No, Madam   \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I  \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO  PARTS (b) AND (c)  OF THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 195 FOR ANSWER ON 24.12.2018 REGARDING “IRREGULARITIES BY \nSCHOOL MANAGEMENT” SHOWING DETAILS OF COMPLAINTS AND ACTION TAKEN \nTHEREOF DURING THE  LAST THREE YEARS \n  \nSl. No Affiliation \nNo. \nDetails of \nSchools \nNature of the \ncomplaint \nComplaint \ndate Action taken \n 1630884. Police DAV \nPublic School \nAffiliation no.  \nFee hike in the \nschool in the name \nof building fund and \nannual charges. \n18.05.2016 The complaint stands \ndisposed of. \n 2730015 DPS \nMathu\nra \nRoad, \nNew \nDelhi \nComplaint against \nthe school for \nhiking the annual \nfee by 15% to 20% \nfrom April 2016. \n10.06.2016 The complaint stands \ndisposed of. \n 2730237 Delhi Public \nSchool, \nSector C, \nPocket V, \nVasant Kunj, \nNew Delhi-\n110070. \nunjustified fees \ntaken by the school \n10.11.2016 \n \nThe complaint stands \ndisposed of. \n 2730487 N K Bagrodia \nPublic School, \nSector 4, \nDwarka, New \nDelhi-110075. \n \ncollecting illegally, \nmaliciously building \nfunds every quarter \nand twelve months \nbus fees from all \nthe students \nstudying in their \nschools \n06.02.2017 The complaint stands \ndis